# VPS self-host
- Public internet: 80/443 only, plus SSH key-only on 22. Do not publish Postgres, Redis, Ollama, admin UIs, or metrics on `0.0.0.0`.
- Do not open a port on production to test. Assume public endpoints are already probed.
- Every Compose service has a memory limit (CPU/pids when practical).
- TLS at the reverse proxy. Rate-limit and block obvious scan headers there. Reject `x-middleware-subrequest`. Do not expose `/metrics` or debug without auth or an allowlist.
- Patch edge frameworks (ASP.NET, Next.js, Nginx, Postgres images) promptly.
- Host facts: `05-product-cms.mdc`.
